Third-party material included in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

app/src/main/aidl/com/bluebubbles/messaging/*.aidl

    Six AIDL interface definitions, copied unmodified from the OpenBubbles
    project:

        https://github.com/OpenBubbles/OpenBubbles
        android/app/src/main/aidl/com/bluebubbles/messaging/

    Copyright the OpenBubbles contributors, licensed under the Apache License,
    Version 2.0.

    These files define the Binder interface an extension must implement in order
    to be bound by OpenBubbles. They are the host's own published interface, and
    they are included here for the same reason a client includes a protocol
    header: an interface definition has to be byte-identical on both sides of
    the wire or the bind fails at runtime.

gradlew, gradlew.bat, gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

    The Gradle wrapper, copyright the Gradle authors, licensed under the Apache
    License, Version 2.0. Build tooling, not project content.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Material deliberately NOT included
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains no OpenPigeon source code, game logic, artwork, audio,
Godot project data, or native libraries, and it is not a fork of OpenPigeon.

OpenPigeon is distributed under PolyForm Shield 1.0.0 with a separate asset
license that does not permit redistribution of its assets in any form. Rather
than vendor that material, OpenSeagull loads the code and resources it needs
from the copy of OpenPigeon already installed on the user's own device, at
runtime. OpenSeagull is useless without OpenPigeon installed, by construction.

That claim is enforced mechanically, not merely asserted:

  - WireContractTest.shippedSourceDeclaresNoOpenPigeonPackage fails the build if
    any file under app/src/main declares an OpenPigeon package.
  - RuntimeHostProbe.weShipNoOpenPigeonCode fails on-device if OpenPigeon
    classes turn out to be loadable from our own APK.

All OpenSeagull artwork (res/drawable/seagull_mark.xml and the icons built from
it) is original to this project.
